From 7ac7b96ed8fb93fa257ee716e6edd4b1552ee886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:39:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 112/116] MAS local: a rotate button on the lean title bar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The lean window was always landscape: the manager fixes the guest's
display to user_rotation 0 (`wm fixed-to-user-rotation enabled`), so a
portrait app sat small between black bars, and the emulator's own rotate
(`emu rotate`, the full toolbar's rotate keys) turned the window but not
the picture. The title bar now has 旋转屏幕 right left of back (after
screenshot and volume): a click turns between landscape (0) and a quarter
turn clockwise, and back.

- The window turns the way the full toolbar's ROTATE_LEFT / ROTATE_RIGHT
  turn it: the device's coarse orientation through the sensors agent,
  which the virtual sensors page passes on to rotateSkin. From 180 or 270
  (console rotate) the button goes back to 0.
- The guest's picture turns with it over adb, `settings put system
  user_rotation N` (ROTATION_270 for the quarter turn clockwise, 0 back),
  on the AdbInterface's own thread. The display stays fixed to the user
  rotation: it still follows neither the sensors nor apps, only the
  button. Nothing is kept across boots: the emulator starts at 0 from
  hw.initialOrientation and the manager sets user_rotation 0 at each
  boot.
- adb as for the volume button: only the server ANDROID_ADB_SERVER_PORT
  names, never 5037; without it, or without adb, the button is disabled
  and says why on hover. Otherwise no hover tip, as for the other title
  bar buttons; its accessible name is 旋转屏幕.
- The window turns with the guest screen at the same scale, keeps its
  centre, is scaled down when it no longer fits the screen's work area,
  and is moved back onto it (fitInto() and placeKeepingCenter() in
  lean-window-frame). A maximized or snapped window keeps its place and
  has the turned guest screen fitted into it, as before.

The full toolbar (ANDROID_EMU_FULL_TOOLBAR=1) is unchanged.

Test: aemu-ui-lean-window_unittests (55, 10 new: the items' order, the
button's target, the user rotation, the adb arguments, fitting and
placing the turned window).

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#225

Change-Id: If63c4345341dbfcc3492b569ecee6e37f4f9377d
